    <fr:title text="(W): the wall conjecture">(W): the wall conjecture</fr:title>
    <fr:taxon>conjecture</fr:taxon>
    <fr:meta name="area">frontier</fr:meta>
    <fr:meta name="avatar">3</fr:meta>
    <fr:meta name="status">refuted</fr:meta>
  </fr:frontmatter>
  <fr:mainmatter>
    <html:p>(W). At every nonvacuous component of the Springer-fiber atlas,
the derived image of the second-level piece in the symplectic quotient
is Lagrangian.</html:p>
    <html:p><html:strong>Role in the skeleton.</html:strong> This was the thesis at the infinitesimal scale — the local form of
<fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0010/" title="(*): the characteristic-p subvariety inference" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0010/" display-uri="ffi-0010" type="local">(*)</fr:link>, upgrading the coisotropy of <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0017/" title="Wall 1: coisotropy of the cyclic cocycle" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0017/" display-uri="ffi-0017" type="local">Wall 1</fr:link>
to equality.</html:p>
    <html:p><html:strong>Status.</html:strong> <html:strong>Refuted</html:strong>, characteristic-free, from <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[n = 6]]></fr:tex>: the
derived image is <html:em>always</html:em> isotropic, never Lagrangian, so the wall
identity cannot hold at component-generic germs. The salvage conjectures
went with it — universal (W-iso) and (C2) are dead, and multi-row
components are all-Lagrangian for a reason that does not generalize. The
twelfth and thirteenth passes closed the wall program.</html:p>
    <html:p><html:strong>Consequence.</html:strong> What the program left behind is the stable depth law: caps,
balanced runs, and donate-2-to-nearest, verified 30/30. That, not the
wall, is the surviving structure at germ scale.</html:p>
    <html:p><html:em>Uses:</html:em> <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0013/" title="The thesis: every bound is half an orbit dimension" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0013/" display-uri="ffi-0013" type="local">The thesis: every bound is half an orbit dimension</fr:link>, <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0017/" title="Wall 1: coisotropy of the cyclic cocycle" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0017/" display-uri="ffi-0017" type="local">Wall 1: coisotropy of the cyclic cocycle</fr:link>, <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0049/" title="The germ apparatus" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0049/" display-uri="ffi-0049" type="local">The germ apparatus</fr:link>.</html:p>
    <html:p>
      <html:em>Provenance: journal passes 12--13; scratch_twelfth, scratch_thirteenth.</html:em>
    </html:p>
  </fr:mainmatter>
